      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T23:48:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "__attribute__((constructor)) functions are not executed in Chrome EC bare-metal firmware (ec-legacy). In core/cortex_m/init.S, application_start zeroes .bss, copies .data, calls system_chip_init, and jumps directly to main(). It does not invoke __libc_init_array or execute functions in .init_array. Consequently, check_canary_before_pre_init() never runs, canary_found_before_pre_init remains false (zeroed in .bss), and TEST_ASSERT(!canary_found_before_pre_init) always passes unconditionally. Furthermore, system_pre_init() clears .ahb4 on boot before tests run, so the subsequent TEST_ASSERT_MEMSET(fp_buffer, 0, ...) also passes. As written, this test cannot verify that system_reset() cleared fp_buffer before resetting.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "536139eaeb0b0e33b3e353915ff877709d621dbb",
